  "notes": "The DigitallyDefined project is a full-stack digital business operating system deployed on Vercel. The backend is a Node.js/TypeScript serverless application with 30+ API endpoints handling social media publishing, Notion integration, AI-powered business intelligence (via Hermes MCP and Groq), email marketing (Brevo/SendPulse), e-commerce (Gumroad), and scheduled cron jobs. The frontend is a React + Vite + Tailwind CSS SPA with Firebase authentication, Supabase database integration, and Vercel analytics. The system integrates with 20+ external services including all major social platforms (Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn, Threads, TikTok, YouTube, Pinterest), Notion for content management, Google Sheets for data sync, and multiple AI providers (Groq, OpenRouter, ZAI, Nous). The Hermes MCP server (Python-based) provides advanced AI agent capabilities. The architecture follows a modern Jamstack pattern with serverless functions, edge deployment, and comprehensive environment variable management for multi-service orchestration."
